Package: BiHeat
Type: Package
Title: Diagonally Split Heatmaps for Paired Matrix Visualization
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person(
    "Gilles", "Colling",
    email = "gilles.colling051@gmail.com",
    role = c("aut", "cre"),
    comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0003-3070-6066"))
Description: Visualizes two numeric matrices of identical shape in a single
    heatmap by splitting each cell along a diagonal. The upper triangle encodes
    one matrix (default white to red) and the lower triangle encodes the other
    (default white to blue). Useful for compact paired comparisons such as
    observed vs. predicted, mean vs. variance, correlation vs. significance,
    or train vs. test performance. Built on 'ggplot2'.
